      "final_text": "Done. `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` on all 5 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\nWhat was wrong and fixed: `VyperSqrt.sqrt` in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) returned the last Babylonian iterate, which can round up (raw `9999999998` \u2192 `9999999999`). It now returns the deployed loop followed by the minimum of the last two iterates (the v0.4.1 fix): `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)`.\n\nProof outline in the file:\n- Nat-level Newton iteration `iter` for `N = a\u00b710\u00b9\u2070` from seed `a/2 + 5\u00b710\u2079`; seed exceeds the root (completed square via `grind` on the two polynomial cases).\n- Error-halving induction gives error \u2264 2 after 167 steps and \u2264 1 after 168 steps, using the library's `newton_sub_sqrt_le_half`, `newton_le_sqrt_add_one`, and `min_newton_eq_sqrt`.\n- A loop-unrolling lemma connects the Int `loop` to the Nat iterates (all operations stay in decimal range), plus a stability lemma for pairs at/below root+1, yielding `sqrt \u2191a = some \u2191\u221a(a\u00b710\u00b9\u2070)`.\n- The three rounding/total requirements follow by casting `Nat.sqrt_le` / `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`; neg-reverts and deployed-loop are direct.\n\nCheck: 2001 property-test cases pass, all six kernels accept, axioms within the permitted set. Passport: `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`5258985a\u2026e50b`).",
